      "writtenOn": "2023-03-28T21:55:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t this be added to all the versions of `clock_enable_module` in `chip`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "73aab4bb2eb443f4cdbc9b2088505b80289fbfc6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "346413bc_1f87f508",
        "filename": "chip/host/clock.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1293547
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-29T05:54:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Adding this to all the versions of `clock_enable_module` is dangerous.\nBecause the compiler would not warn you if you link two weak symbols at the same time.\nAnd the final result will depend on the file order we put in the linker stage.",
      "parentUuid": "37026100_f1c284ff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "73aab4bb2eb443f4cdbc9b2088505b80289fbfc6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "732a66be_a09fd605",
        "filename": "chip/host/clock.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1293547
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-29T05:57:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "And we already do the same thing to `test_mockable timestamp_t get_time(void)`. (Only mock the host version.)",
      "parentUuid": "346413bc_1f87f508",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "73aab4bb2eb443f4cdbc9b2088505b80289fbfc6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "afd1feb5_51b7df75",
        "filename": "chip/host/clock.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-30T17:20:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e not warn you if you link two weak symbols at the same time\n\nWhere is the second weak version of `clock_enable_module`? The host version won\u0027t be linked with the version built for the EC, and only a single `chip` is built for a given EC board.",
      "parentUuid": "732a66be_a09fd605",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "73aab4bb2eb443f4cdbc9b2088505b80289fbfc6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c9ea4f8_dea88d80",
        "filename": "chip/host/clock.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1293547
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-30T17:56:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We will not have two weak symbols \"now\".\n\nBut if we add test_mockable to every chip, if someone wants to change the chip code in the future, it may easily be screwed up. \n\ne.g. You can take a look at the complex `#if #elif #else #endif` macros in `chip/npcx/clock.c`.",
      "parentUuid": "afd1feb5_51b7df75",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "73aab4bb2eb443f4cdbc9b2088505b80289fbfc6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8d65c04_ae00b942",
        "filename": "chip/host/clock.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1293547
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-31T07:34:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After consulting with @phoenixshen, we think adding `test_mockable` to all the versions of `clock_enable_module` is not a good idea.",
      "parentUuid": "1c9ea4f8_dea88d80",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "73aab4bb2eb443f4cdbc9b2088505b80289fbfc6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66bdc0e4_74b632d0",
        "filename": "chip/host/clock.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-06T23:44:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e But if we add test_mockable to every chip, if someone wants to change the chip code in the future, it may easily be screwed up.\n\u003e e.g. You can take a look at the complex #if #elif #else #endif macros in chip/npcx/clock.c.\n\nI\u0027m not sure I follow the reasoning. Yes, there are lot of `#ifdef`\u0027s in `chip/npcx/clock.c`, which is bad. Are you concerned that the mock will somehow be included in the release build? The [mock framework](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/HEAD/common/mock/README.md) was specifically designed to [only affect the test and fuzzer builds](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/Makefile;l\u003d199-208;drc\u003d12e1ed299bf8a1323702fe44cff6a16c36a5d644) and the [mock can easily verify this](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/mock/timer_mock.c;l\u003d8-10;drc\u003d71b2ef709dcb14260f5fdaa3ab4ced005a29fb46).",
      "parentUuid": "b8d65c04_ae00b942",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "73aab4bb2eb443f4cdbc9b2088505b80289fbfc6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c626c61d_fe93e90a",
        "filename": "chip/host/clock.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
