      "writtenOn": "2023-04-07T02:07:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My concern is we might accidentally define multiple weak instances of `clock_enable_module` in the test build(e.g. device tests) in the future.\n\nAnd I don\u0027t even know how to fix the linker issue in zephyr build now.\n\n```\n/opt/coreboot-sdk/lib/gcc/riscv64-elf/11.2.0/../../../../riscv64-elf/bin/ld.bfd: /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/geralt/modules/ec/common/vboot_hash.c:185: undefined reference to `clock_enable_module\u0027\ncollect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status\nExecution failed (return code\u003d1): /usr/bin/ninja -C /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/geralt/build-ro\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/zephyr/zmake/zmake/multiproc.py\", line 379, in _run_fn\n    result \u003d func()\n  File \"/mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/zephyr/zmake/zmake/zmake.py\", line 815, in _build_one_dir\n    raise OSError(get_process_failure_msg(proc))\nOSError: Execution failed (return code\u003d1): /usr/bin/ninja -C /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/geralt/build-ro\n...\n```\n\nLooks like zephyr have different source of chip definitions in zephyr.",
      "parentUuid": "66bdc0e4_74b632d0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 13
      },
